Subject: [202605] Increase AS7326 Broadcom SDK stable storage

Increase AS7326 stable_size from 85 MiB to 128 MiB for SDK 6.5.35-SP1.
The older 88 MiB workaround from PR #22641 still exhausted scache:
max=92274688, used=92082660, alloc_size=1361924, then extender init failed.
Direct initialization and normal syncd/SWSS startup succeeded at 128 MiB
on our BCM56873_A0 test switch; all 56 front-panel ports became visible.
Use the SDK-provided Cancun default symlink instead of the absent 6.4.1 path,
matching the tested configuration (default pointed to b870.6.15.0).
Keep this scoped to AS7326; do not change other platforms or SDK binaries.

Upstream issue: https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-buildimage/issues/21295
Earlier workaround: https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-buildimage/pull/22641
Verified source: de9703231aa99a5173f37825a1b120aa602f1a26.
Remove when upstream includes this setting or a replacement SDK configuration.

Tested with SAI 15.2.1.0.0.0.50.1 on 2026-11-12. Reboot persistence,
forwarding, VXLAN and warm restart still require validation. 128 MiB is a
working allocation, not a measured minimum or a guarantee for all workloads.

--- a/device/accton/x86_64-accton_as7326_56x-r0/Accton-AS7326-56X/td3-as7326-48x25G+8x100G.config.bcm
+++ b/device/accton/x86_64-accton_as7326_56x-r0/Accton-AS7326-56X/td3-as7326-48x25G+8x100G.config.bcm
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-sai_load_hw_config=/etc/bcm/flex/bcm56870_a0_premium_issu/b870.6.4.1/
+sai_load_hw_config=/etc/bcm/flex/bcm56870_a0_premium_issu/default/
 #polarity/lanemap is using TH2 style.
 core_clock_frequency=1525
 dpp_clock_ratio=2:3
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@
 module_64ports=1
 port_flex_enable=1
 schan_intr_enable=0
-stable_size=0x5500000
+stable_size=0x8000000
 tdma_timeout_usec=3000000
 skip_L2_USER_ENTRY=0
 bcm_tunnel_term_compatible_mode=1
